<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027035817 +0000" stop="20261027042825 +0000">
    <title>Around the World in 80 Tricks S1 - "Delhi"</title>
    <desc>In this episode Pete take to the streets of India’s capital city Delhi. He performs a series of fun and baffling tricks including a levitation attempt.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027042825 +0000" stop="20261027045844 +0000">
    <title>Around the World in 80 Tricks S1 - "Delhi &amp; Mumbai"</title>
    <desc>Pete is in Delhi and Mumbai performing magic to a variety of people, including a baffling thirst quenching trick, as well as making rings and himself vanish!</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027045844 +0000" stop="20261027060000 +0000">
    <title>Ultimate Processes S1 - "Bikes"</title>
    <desc>We are in the middle of a cycling revolution and these days there’s a bike for every occasion, so presenter Francesca Chiorando tries out two of them.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027060000 +0000" stop="20261027061245 +0000">
    <title>Science of Sound S1 - "Live Music Vibes"</title>
    <desc>It’s easy to love live music. Whether you’re jamming with some friends or you’re lost in the crowd at an amazing show, live music really moves us. But why does it feel so much better than listening to music on the best home stereo?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027061245 +0000" stop="20261027062531 +0000">
    <title>Science of Sound S1 - "Untrained Ears"</title>
    <desc>It’s no surprise that trained musicians experience music differently than others. Sure, musicians can hear and recognize similar chords or melodies across different songs, but is that all?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027062531 +0000" stop="20261027063947 +0000">
    <title>Science of Sound S1 - "Developing Our Taste in Music"</title>
    <desc>In the era of music streaming, there are millions of songs at our fingertips. But in a world of near infinite music choices, music discovery and exposure have changed drastically.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027063947 +0000" stop="20261027070828 +0000">
    <title>The Re-Inventors S3 - "Battering Ram"</title>
    <desc>The invention of the battering ram was a breakthrough thousands of years ago, but does it still pack a punch?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027070828 +0000" stop="20261027073711 +0000">
    <title>The Re-Inventors S3 - "Chinese War Kite"</title>
    <desc>Join Matt and Jeremy as they combine 13th century Chinese fire arrow technology with a 17th century Japanise kite design to see if they can command the battlefield with this amazing device.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027073711 +0000" stop="20261027080554 +0000">
    <title>The Re-Inventors S3 - "Pedestrian Protectoc"</title>
    <desc>Can we protect both pedestrians and drivers? Watch this episode to find out.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027080554 +0000" stop="20261027083437 +0000">
    <title>The Re-Inventors S3 - "Aerosan"</title>
    <desc>Did the soviets invent an invincible snowmobile? Let's see.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027083437 +0000" stop="20261027092919 +0000">
    <title>Dictators' Hideouts S1 - "Hitler's Last Secret"</title>
    <desc>Thanks to secret, recently discovered microfilm, Hitler's last secret is revealed: a sprawling underground headquarters at Książ Castle.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027092919 +0000" stop="20261027102402 +0000">
    <title>Dictators' Hideouts S1 - "Mussolini's Underground Refuge"</title>
    <desc>50 km north of Rome lies the greatest hideout in fascist Italy’s history: The Monte Soratte Bunker, with security features even a Bond villain could only dream of.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027102402 +0000" stop="20261027111844 +0000">
    <title>Dictators' Hideouts S1 - "Hoxha's Bunker Madness"</title>
    <desc>Paranoid and isolated, Albanian dictator Enver Hoxha establishes his bunkerization project, which would result in the construction of more than 170,000 bunkers.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027111844 +0000" stop="20261027121427 +0000">
    <title>Dictators' Hideouts S1 - "Stalin's Atomic Bunker"</title>
    <desc>Infamous for the bunkers constructed during World War II and throughout the Cold War, Stalin’s hideouts have maintained a shroud of secrecy for decades, and are now seen for the first time.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027121427 +0000" stop="20261027124204 +0000">
    <title>How Do They Do It S13 - "Crystal Glass/Flat Screen TVs/Deepest Pool/Ketchup"</title>
    <desc>How do they blow the world’s finest crystal wine glasses? How do they make the world’s slimmest TVs? How do they heat the world’s deepest swimming pool? How do they fill a million bottles a day of the world’s favourite ketchup?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027124204 +0000" stop="20261027130940 +0000">
    <title>How Do They Do It S13 - "Pulverizer/Bomber Jackets/Lambic Beer/"</title>
    <desc>How do they forge a set of jaws that can chomp through concrete and demolish tower blocks? How do they stitch the historic airman’s bomber? How do they brew the oldest beer in the Western World?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027130940 +0000" stop="20261027133706 +0000">
    <title>How Do They Do It S13 - "Sydney Opera House/Handsaws/Microphones/Icebreaker"</title>
    <desc>How do they cool Sydney’s famous Opera House? How do they turn Sheffield steel into a carpenter’s handsaw? How do they make a microphone that can pick up a whisper? How do they steer a safe course through a frozen river?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027133706 +0000" stop="20261027140435 +0000">
    <title>How Do They Do It S13 - "Moonshine/e-bikes/Wetsuits"</title>
    <desc>How do they brew moonshine in the heart of New York City? How do they make a battery powered bicycle that can do nearly 30mph? How do they grow the rubber for wetsuits in the Arizona desert?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027140435 +0000" stop="20261027150634 +0000">
    <title>Destruction Decoded S1 - "Megafloods"</title>
    <desc>Witness the devastating destructive power unleashed by planet earth’s most valuable resource – water.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027150634 +0000" stop="20261027161021 +0000">
    <title>Destruction Decoded S1 - "Constructions"</title>
    <desc>Discover the worst bridge collapses and tunnel fires in history.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027161021 +0000" stop="20261027171246 +0000">
    <title>Destruction Decoded S1 - "Hurricanes"</title>
    <desc>Explore with us one of the most destructive and deadliest hurricanes in history!</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027171246 +0000" stop="20261027181609 +0000">
    <title>Destruction Decoded S1 - "Earthquakes"</title>
    <desc>Explore with us the most destructive earthquakes in history, can we even protect ourselves from this natural disaster?</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027181609 +0000" stop="20261027191154 +0000">
    <title>War Factories S3 - "Skoda: the factory that fought back"</title>
    <desc>In 1939 Nazi Germany seized Czechoslovakia’s Škoda Works.But under A.Göring’s covert resistance, the factory was used to undermine the Nazi war effort.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027191154 +0000" stop="20261027200746 +0000">
    <title>War Factories S3 - "Ferdinand Porsche: Nazi muscle machines"</title>
    <desc>Ferdinand Porsche designed major Nazi vehicles including the Tiger tank and VW Kübelwagen, but many impractical designs strained Germany’s war effort.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027200746 +0000" stop="20261027210303 +0000">
    <title>War Factories S3 - "Opel: The truck that ran the Blitzkrieg"</title>
    <desc>Modern warfare depended on logistics, and the Opel Blitz truck powered Nazi Blitzkrieg—despite being owned by an American company.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027210303 +0000" stop="20261027215902 +0000">
    <title>War Factories S3 - "War Machine: The story of the machine-gun"</title>
    <desc>A history of the machine gun, from the Gatling to the MG42, and the factories that drove its development.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027215902 +0000" stop="20261027222702 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Live Fire Exercises, Body Armor, Armored Vehicle AJAX"</title>
    <desc>Discover the latest innovations in kit and equipment at the key military and security exhibition in the UK; Lockheed Martin's heat-seeking Indago drone; and the tech spec on the British Army's new armored vehicle, the AJAX.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027222702 +0000" stop="20261027225445 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Battlefield 3-D, Drone Tech, 2-man Orcasub"</title>
    <desc>The innovative combination of 3D video and drone technology gives infantry soldiers an accurate battlefield picture. Northrop Grumman's top European executive shares their predictions on how technology will change the way we fight.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027225445 +0000" stop="20261027232237 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "USS Zumwalt, Tank Training, Special Forces Vehicle"</title>
    <desc>We reveal eye-witness intelligence on the USS Zumwalt, America's ultra-hi tech, four billion dollar guided missile destroyer. Learn more about the British firm who've developed Minerva, an ingenious, low-cost but realistic tank simulator.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027232237 +0000" stop="20261027235037 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Typhoon Fighter, Combat Medics, USS Dwight D. Eisenhower"</title>
    <desc>The Military Tech Show captures the moment when BAE System's radical new pilot helmet, the Striker II, goes operational for the first time in a Typhoon fighter aircraft; how interactive technology is helping train military combat medics.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261027235037 +0000" stop="20261028005224 +0000">
    <title>Cold War: The Tech Race S1 - "Information Is Power"</title>
    <desc>Cold War secrecy accelerates spy tech, satellite surveillance, and early computer networks, laying the foundation for modern global communications.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-62f42e6cad0081c6ef405723" start="20261027040838 +0000" stop="20261027060801 +0000">
    <title>The House From...</title>
    <desc>Exploring the lives of owners of iconic TV and movie homes, and how nostalgia reshapes them.</desc>
  </programme>
  
